  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-168842638426899e3410/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>Michael Rudden</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2024-05-06T15:47:45-04:00\" title=\"Monday, May 6, 2024, 3:47 pm\">May 6, 2024</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t<p>The Guild of Harwich Artists held a ‘Harwich Herring Run’ community painting event during last weekend’s ArtWeek 2024 at the Arts &amp; Cultural Center.  Members of the Guild helped folks of all ages to paint precut canvas fish to create a large mural of a herring run.  Using shades of blue paint and a wide variety of texture creating tools participants added buttons for eyes and hung their fish on the mural.<img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-7047\" src=\"/media/archive/dc176b5852440613b7ce97a9f26f5f190562c4fa862f39900847a1daba49a1cd.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /> <img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-7048\" src=\"/media/archive/698a40a15330acc157eea3782a9d279b55076149106deb8d181ce1ffe4cf73ee.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"142\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<footer class=\"entry-footer\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-terms category\">Posted in <a href=\"/archive/source-e23b79be08a822c7b682/\" rel=\"tag\">WHAT'S NEW</a></span>\t\t\t\t\t</footer>\n\n\t\n",
